# L §4.4, §5.18 (tally 2.1.8 R13, #169-d; P29): under windows each a line's binding is read inside each run, so a
# tuple bound over only some sub-windows of a window its binding reads prints under those, with their head. d[a] is
# 2026-03-01 or 2026-03-02: `where d[k] < 2026-03-02` binds a only on the first day (q1, q3), `where d[k] >
# 2026-03-01` only on the second (p1); a movement dated on the window wd is bound over April only while wd falls in
# it (qw). 2.1.7's refcore bound once, reading each window as its first day: q1 (k = a) had no head, p1 left a out,
# qw printed nothing.
=== m.tally
model px
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place work: outside lives 1900-01-01..

index kk = [a, b]
input d[k in kk]: date
input e[k in kk]: date
input wd: date
input amt: money PLN

move g: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from work to konto amount amt

ask q1: e[k] < 2026-03-02 for k in kk where d[k] < 2026-03-02 windows each
ask p1: e[k] < 2026-03-02 for k in kk where d[k] > 2026-03-01 windows each
ask q3: d[k] for k in kk where d[k] < 2026-03-02 windows each
ask qw: m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-30 windows each

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "c"
  d[a] = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-02) "c"
  d[b] = 2026-01-01 "c"
  e[a] = 2026-01-01 "c"
  e[b] = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-02) "c"
  wd = window(2026-03-30, 2026-04-02) "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "own"
=== expect
p1 (k = a) [d[a] = 2026-03-02]: true
  cut 2026-03-01
q1 (k = a) [d[a] = 2026-03-01]: true
  cut 2026-03-01
q1 (k = b) [e[b] = 2026-03-01]: true
  cut 2026-03-01
q1 (k = b) [e[b] = 2026-03-02]: false
  cut 2026-03-01
q3 (k = a) [d[a] = 2026-03-01]: 2026-03-01
  cut 2026-03-01
q3 (k = b): 2026-01-01
  cut 2026-03-01
qw (m = g) [wd = 2026-04-01 .. 2026-04-02]: 10.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
